+
+# 9. Security Tests
+
+Mandatory automated checks:
+
+```text
+non-loopback internal observatory request        403
+forwarded/proxied observatory request            403
+browser mutation method                          rejected
+principalId in any UI JSON                       0
+memory lease token in any UI JSON                0
+GitHub token in any UI JSON                      0
+Memory Remote key in any UI JSON                 0
+OAuth token in any UI JSON                       0
+raw authorization/cookie headers                 0
+hidden/private reasoning field                   0
+public port-3697 visibility mutation             0
+```
+
+Also scan bundled frontend output for known synthetic secret fixtures used by tests.
+
+---
+
+# 10. Failure Policy
+
+## UI process fails
+
+```text
+UI unavailable
+memory remains healthy
+activity continues in AuditJournal
+restart UI → replay retained activity + snapshot
+```
+
+## SSE connection fails
+
+```text
+browser reconnects with Last-Event-ID
+retained history available → replay
+history gone → explicit gap + snapshot resync
+```
+
+## AuditJournal backpressure/drop
+
+```text
+authoritative memory continues
+metric/drop count increments
+live tracker shows observability degradation when status detects it
+snapshot remains authoritative
+```
+
+## Memory degraded
+
+```text
+UI shows DEGRADED
+must not invent nodes or empty state
+```
+
+## Remote unavailable after prior hydration
+
+```text
+UI shows REMOTE_PENDING / UNAVAILABLE
+local factual graph remains visible
+must not label task cross-Codespace durable
+```
+
+## Fresh runtime hydration fails
+
+```text
+UI shows hydration failure
+must not present an empty graph as confirmed new memory
+```
+
+---
+
+# 11. Cutover State Machine
+
+```text
+PLAN_COMPLETE
+      ↓
+SHADOW_IMPLEMENTED
+      ↓
+SHADOW_STABLE
+      ↓
+ADVISORY_CANARY_STABLE
+      ↓
+ENFORCED_CANARY_STABLE
+      ↓
+CUTOVER_READY
+      ↓
+[EXPLICIT USER AUTHORIZATION]
+      ↓
+LIVE_CUTOVER
+      ↓
+SOAK_VERIFIED
+```
+
+No implementation step may jump from `SHADOW_IMPLEMENTED` directly to `LIVE_CUTOVER`.
+
+---
+
+# 12. Definition of Stable
+
+The Memory Observatory + memory candidate may be called stable only when:
+
+```text
+1. Real memory operations create the expected visible node/revision/edge outcome.
+2. `remember_more` highlights only persisted bounded expansion history.
+3. Every new non-root node has a justified semantic edge.
+4. Every new root exposes its persisted fresh-context reason.
+5. Failure history survives solution/validation.
+6. Browser refresh/restart reproduces the authoritative graph.
+7. SSE disconnect/reconnect neither duplicates nor silently loses retained events.
+8. Audit retention gaps are explicit.
+9. UI crash has zero effect on memory/execution/MCP correctness.
+10. Cross-Codespace deletion/recovery reproduces identical logical memory state.
+11. Remote durability state is truthful in the UI.
+12. Scope isolation remains zero-contamination.
+13. No secret/lease/principal leakage is present.
+14. Existing 100k preflight p95 remains <150 ms.
+15. Observatory overhead and real-time latency meet this plan's gates.
+16. Full Agent Core/Codespace release regression remains green on the exact remote-visible SHA.
+```
+
+Only then may the project advance to controlled live integration.
+
